      "message": "You\u0027ve already got `last_member` which is exactly this (though `last_member` is misleading, see above).\n\nIn fact, resolving the constant value in two different places is also a little confusing. I\u0027m wondering you could fold these two switches together, maybe with a helper lambda to handle the const and non-const offset cases for the non-struct scenario. In fact, `CalculateVectorIndex` is pretty much that helper function, and it\u0027s not really specific to vectors, so maybe just use that?\n\nAlternatively you could just always use a dynamic `mul` instruction and rely on constant folding to clean stuff up the indexing logic later, which would further simplify this code, though I appreciate that it\u0027d make the unit test outputs a little noisier.",
